// The RelationalMapper element: rewrites database, schema and table names on the way to SQL.
//
// This is how one model targets a differently-named physical layout per environment, and it
// is the alternative to the key-based routing in 67-routing-surface.pure -- routing picks a
// RUNTIME, this rewrites the NAMES a single runtime emits.
//
// Its section is QueryPostProcessor, not RelationalMapper: the element is named
// RelationalMapper but its section parser is registered under POSTPROCESSOR_NAME.
//
// It lives in its own file rather than beside the connection that references it. Sharing a
// file, the reference did not resolve in the FULL model -- "Can't find the packageable
// element 'surface::ProdMapper'" -- while the file compiled fine on its own.
###QueryPostProcessor
RelationalMapper surface::ProdMapper
(
   // A DatabaseMapper's brackets hold SCHEMA references (`database DOT schema`), not bare
   // databases. Several schemas can be redirected to one physical database.
   DatabaseMappers:
   [
      [combo::ComboDB.analytics, combo::ComboDB.default] -> 'PROD_WAREHOUSE'
   ];
   SchemaMappers:
   [
      combo::ComboDB.analytics -> 'PROD_ANALYTICS'
   ];
   TableMappers:
   [
      combo::ComboDB.analytics.COMBO_SUMMARY -> 'PROD_SUMMARY'
   ];
)
